import{_ as t,o as s,c as o,an as r}from"./chunks/framework.BU62xgrP.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Structure ratchet and migrations","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"development/structure.md","filePath":"development/structure.md","lastUpdated":null}'),i={name:"development/structure.md"};function a(d,e,n,c,l,h){return s(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r(`<h1 id="Structure-ratchet-and-migrations" tabindex="-1">Structure ratchet and migrations <a class="header-anchor" href="#Structure-ratchet-and-migrations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Structure ratchet and migrations {#Structure-ratchet-and-migrations}&quot;">​</a></h1><p><code>scripts/checks/check_structure.jl</code> parses the include tree with JuliaSyntax and never loads the package. Run it from the checkout root against the branch your change will merge into:</p><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> julia</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --startup-file=no</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --project=test</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> scripts/checks/check_structure.jl</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --base=origin/main</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>src/LAYERS.toml</code> records the allowed module and folder dependency edges, the folder order and reasoned folder-order exceptions. The files in <code>test/structure/</code> snapshot existing debt: duplicate helpers, body clones, private uses, detached docstrings, core-to-non-core uses and oversized folders. Every snapshot may only shrink relative to the base. Editing a snapshot in the same diff cannot grant a new edge or allowance. The order checks use the actual include order and <code>folder_order</code> independently of the ratchet. A folder-order exception is kept only for a reverse edge that the order rules, including module child wiring and shared-module wiring, would otherwise reject.</p><h2 id="Moves,-renames-and-splits" tabindex="-1">Moves, renames and splits <a class="header-anchor" href="#Moves,-renames-and-splits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Moves, renames and splits {#Moves,-renames-and-splits}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Snapshots are keyed by names: module names, folder paths and source file paths. When a change moves code to a new name, it declares each transfer as a reviewed row in <code>test/structure/migrations.toml</code>:</p><div class="language-toml vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">toml</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">[[</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">migration</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">]]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">from = </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;src/Preprocessing&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">to = [</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;src/Preprocessing&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;src/Preprocessing/Core&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;src/Preprocessing/Vertical&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">reason = </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;Split preprocessing into ordered stage folders&quot;</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>from</code> must be a module or folder declared in the base <code>src/LAYERS.toml</code>, or a Julia file of the base. Every <code>to</code> entry must be a current identity of the same kind. In the base snapshots, the checker substitutes the <code>to</code> identities for <code>from</code>:</p><ul><li><p>Each target may use the base dependencies of <code>from</code>, plus its own base dependencies if it already existed. The targets of one row may also use each other: they were one unit before.</p></li><li><p>Base edges to <code>from</code> may now point to any target, so existing users can follow the moved code.</p></li><li><p><code>from</code> keeps its budget and users only if it is listed in <code>to</code>. A vacated name that is later reused starts with no budget; an <code>Empty -&gt; Rich</code> rename gives the new <code>Rich</code> only the old budget of <code>Empty</code>.</p></li><li><p>In allowance ids, only module, folder and file fields follow a row. A file field also follows its folder&#39;s row. Helper names, signatures and digests never change.</p></li><li><p>Each base allowance and folder-order exception moves to at most one place. It is never copied, so these entries cannot grow in number. If a retained <code>from</code> and one of its pieces both need an exception, the second one is a new allowance. Module child wiring already exempts facade edges, so main keeps no exceptions for them that a split could carry to a new folder.</p></li><li><p>The byte ceilings drawn from one base ceiling may not exceed it in sum. Each ceiling must still equal its folder&#39;s current size.</p></li></ul><p>Rows are not chained: a target of one row never receives the budget that another row grants to its <code>from</code>.</p><h3 id="Direction-among-the-pieces" tabindex="-1">Direction among the pieces <a class="header-anchor" href="#Direction-among-the-pieces" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Direction among the pieces {#Direction-among-the-pieces}&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Peer grants are symmetric, so the ordinary order checks decide the direction:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Modules.</strong> A reference to a later module fails. A child module may use its parent, because the parent precedes it in include order. This is the facade usage that <code>LAYERS.toml</code> already contains for many modules.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cycles.</strong> Parent and child wiring is not counted as a module cycle.</p></li><li><p><strong>Folders.</strong> Direction follows the PR&#39;s <code>folder_order</code>. That order is declared, not ratcheted; review it together with the rows.</p></li></ul><h2 id="Row-validation" tabindex="-1">Row validation <a class="header-anchor" href="#Row-validation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Row validation {#Row-validation}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The checker rejects:</p><ul><li><p>rows without a reason or without distinct <code>to</code> identities;</p></li><li><p>a <code>from</code> that is not a base identity, or a target of the wrong kind;</p></li><li><p>an unused row target, whose removal exposes no allowance growth;</p></li><li><p>a target that another row also covers. This is reported as redundant with the other row; keep one.</p></li></ul><p>A row identical to one in the base <code>migrations.toml</code> (same <code>from</code> and <code>to</code>) was applied there and is <strong>inert</strong>. When <code>migrations.toml</code> equals the base copy, as on a clean <code>main</code>, the checker only warns that such rows can be deleted. A pull request that edits <code>migrations.toml</code> must delete them.</p><p>Pull requests compare with their target branch. CI compares a push to <code>main</code> with the commit <code>main</code> had before the push (<code>github.event.before</code>). It falls back to <code>HEAD^1</code> when that commit is all zeros or cannot be fetched. A merge, including a multi-commit rebase merge, therefore validates its rows once more. Afterwards they are inert. No Julia code is specific to a past cleanup.</p><h2 id="Examples" tabindex="-1">Examples <a class="header-anchor" href="#Examples" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Examples {#Examples}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>These rows reproduce the merged folder cleanups against each merge&#39;s first parent. Those trees still carry the facade exceptions that module child wiring makes unneeded; the rows pass once those exceptions are deleted, as on <code>main</code> today.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:right;">Cleanup</th><th style="text-align:right;">Rows</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:right;">X1 #108</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>AtmosTransport.Analysis -&gt; [Analysis, Diagnostics]</code>, <code>src/Analysis -&gt; [src/Extras/Analysis, src/Diagnostics]</code>, <code>src/Diagnostics -&gt; [src]</code> (the timer moves to <code>src</code>), <code>src/Analysis/Analysis.jl -&gt; [src/Diagnostics/Diagnostics.jl]</code>, one row each moving Visualization, Downloads and <code>Downloads/sources</code> into <code>src/Extras</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">O1 #110</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>AtmosTransport.Output -&gt; [Output, Observations, .Retrievals, .Sources, .Sampling]</code>, <code>src/Output/observations -&gt; [Retrievals, Sources, Sampling]</code>, <code>src/Output -&gt; [src/Output, src/Observations]</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">M1 #111</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>AtmosTransport.MetDrivers -&gt; [MetDrivers, .BinaryFormat, .BinaryReaders]</code>, <code>src/MetDrivers/transport_binary -&gt; [BinaryFormat, BinaryReaders]</code>, <code>src/MetDrivers/ERA5 -&gt; [src/Preprocessing/sources]</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">C1 #114</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>AtmosTransport.Operators.Convection</code> and <code>src/Operators/Convection</code>, each to itself plus <code>TM5</code> and <code>CMFMC</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">A1 #115</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>src/Operators/Advection -&gt; [Advection, Reconstruction, Structured, CubedSphere]</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">T1 #116</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>AtmosTransport.Adjoints -&gt; [Adjoints, .Footprint, .Inversion, .Inversion.Observations, .Inversion.Solver]</code>, <code>src/Footprint -&gt; [src/Adjoints/Footprint]</code>, <code>src/Inversion -&gt; [src/Adjoints/Inversion, .../Solver]</code>, <code>src/Adjoints -&gt; [src/Adjoints, src/Adjoints/Inversion/Observations]</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">PP1 #117</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>AtmosTransport.Preprocessing</code> and <code>src/Preprocessing</code>, each to itself plus <code>Core</code>, <code>Vertical</code> and <code>Spectral</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">PP2 #118</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>AtmosTransport.Preprocessing</code> and <code>src/Preprocessing</code>, each to itself plus <code>MassClosure</code> and <code>PhysicsInputs</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">MD1 #119</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>src/Models -&gt; [src/Models, Physics, Core, Runner]</code>, <code>src/Models/runner -&gt; [src/Models/Runner]</code>, <code>src/Models/initial_conditions -&gt; [src/Models/InitialConditions]</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="Shared-module-folder-wiring" tabindex="-1">Shared-module folder wiring <a class="header-anchor" href="#Shared-module-folder-wiring" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Shared-module folder wiring {#Shared-module-folder-wiring}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Folder edges must point to earlier folders unless <code>folder_order_allow</code> records an exception. Two wiring cases are exempt:</p><ul><li><p>A module entry file may include or re-export child modules in its subfolders.</p></li><li><p>Two named layouts share one module across folders:</p><ul><li><p><code>src/Operators/Advection</code> may wire its <code>Reconstruction</code>, <code>Structured</code> and <code>CubedSphere</code> folders.</p></li><li><p>The Models folders may wire each other where they share <code>AtmosTransport.Models</code>.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p>Sibling order and all external dependencies still follow the ordinary rules.</p>`,25)])])}const g=t(i,[["render",a]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
